from pathlib import Path
from decimal import Decimal
import json
from reportlab.pdfgen import canvas
from reportlab.lib.pagesizes import letter

root=Path('demo-data')
manifest={'synthetic':True,'notice':'Entirely fictional demonstration fixtures. No real people, properties, agreements or invoices.','users':10,'departments':4,'agents':4,'invoices':[],'hr_documents':[],'legal_documents':[],'property_listings':30,'example_workflows':10,'historical_workflow_runs':15,'historical_notice':'Historical workflow records are generated by app.seed and labeled seeded demonstration data, never live executions.'}
for number in range(1,21):
 subtotal=Decimal(850+number*75)
 tax=(subtotal*Decimal('0.08')).quantize(Decimal('0.01'))
 item={'vendor_name':f'Fictional Property Services {number:02d}','invoice_number':f'DEMO-INV-{number:04d}','invoice_date':'2026-09-15','due_date':'2026-10-15','currency':'USD','subtotal':str(subtotal.quantize(Decimal('0.01'))),'tax':str(tax),'total':str(subtotal+tax),'line_items':[{'description':f'Fictional property inspection {number:02d}','quantity':'1','unit_price':str(subtotal.quantize(Decimal('0.01'))),'amount':str(subtotal.quantize(Decimal('0.01')))}]}
 path=root/'invoices'/f'invoice-{number:02d}.pdf'
 pdf=canvas.Canvas(str(path),pagesize=letter, pageCompression=0, invariant=1)
 pdf.setTitle(f'Synthetic invoice {item["invoice_number"]}')
 pdf.setAuthor('EnterpriseFlow AI synthetic fixture generator')
 lines=['FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION INVOICE — NOT PAYABLE',f'Vendor: {item["vendor_name"]}','Customer: Fictional Marketplace Laboratory',f'Invoice number: {item["invoice_number"]}',f'Invoice date: {item["invoice_date"]}',f'Due date: {item["due_date"]}',f'Currency: {item["currency"]}','',item['line_items'][0]['description'],f'Quantity: 1 | Unit price: {item["subtotal"]} | Amount: {item["subtotal"]}',f'Subtotal: {item["subtotal"]}',f'Tax (8%): {item["tax"]}',f'Total: {item["total"]}','','All entities and transactions are synthetic. No payment should be made.']
 for i,line in enumerate(lines):pdf.drawString(45,750-i*24,line)
 pdf.save()
 manifest['invoices'].append({'path':str(path.relative_to(root)), 'expected':item})
policies=[
 ('vacation-policy','Vacation Policy','Eligible full-time employees receive 20 paid vacation days per calendar year. Requests must be submitted to the department manager at least 10 business days before the requested start. A maximum of five unused days may carry forward until March 31. This policy does not state any other leave entitlement.'),
 ('onboarding-policy','Onboarding Policy','The manager assigns an onboarding buddy before the start date. New starters complete identity verification, security training, device setup, and benefits orientation during their first five business days. The manager reviews the checklist on day ten. Sensitive identity documents belong in restricted HR storage.'),
 ('benefits-guide','Benefits Guide','The fictional company benefits portal provides plan summaries. New employees schedule benefits orientation with HR within 30 days of joining. This synthetic policy contains no medical recommendations, real insurance terms, or financial benefits promises.'),
 ('remote-work','Remote Work Policy','Eligible roles may request up to two remote days per week with manager approval. Company documents must remain in approved systems. Public computers may not access confidential employee records.'),
 ('security-training','Security Training Policy','All employees complete annual security training and phishing awareness. New employees finish the introductory module during onboarding. Report suspicious messages to the internal security queue; never send passwords or tokens in a support ticket.'),
 ('equipment-return','Equipment Return Policy','Departing employees return issued laptops, access badges, and security keys to Operations. HR records the completed return checklist. A manager verifies all assigned equipment items within two business days.'),
 ('expense-policy','Expense Submission Policy','Employees submit a receipt, business purpose, date, and currency for each expense. Managers review department expenses before Finance records the decision. This workflow does not issue reimbursements or transfer funds.'),
 ('document-retention','HR Document Retention Policy','HR classifies records before storage. Restricted employee documents are visible only to explicitly authorized people. Removal requests require an approved retention review. This synthetic example does not define legally required retention periods.'),
 ('learning-development','Learning and Development Policy','Employees may request a fictional annual learning allowance of 500 USD. The manager reviews job relevance before approving a training request. No external purchase is automatically executed by the workflow.'),
 ('manager-review','Manager Review Policy','Managers review onboarding task completion and supporting evidence. A reviewer must be authorized for the same department. A decision records reviewer identity, timestamp, comments, and final status. Delegation requires an explicit membership update.'),
]
for i,(slug,title,text) in enumerate(policies,1):
 path=root/'hr'/f'{i:02d}-{slug}.md'
 path.write_text(f'# {title}\n\n**Synthetic demonstration policy — no actual employment terms.**\n\nDepartment: Human Resources\nVersion: 1.0\nEffective date: 2026-01-01\n\n{text}\n')
 manifest['hr_documents'].append({'path':str(path.relative_to(root)),'title':title,'department':'hr'})
for i in range(1,11):
 path=root/'legal'/f'agreement-{i:02d}.md'
 text=f'''# Fictional Service Agreement {i:02d}

**SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION AGREEMENT — NOT BINDING**

Parties: Fictional Marketplace Laboratory and Imaginary Vendor {i:02d}.
Effective date: 2026-10-01. Termination date: 2027-10-01.
Document type: service_agreement. Currency: USD.

## Services and obligations

Imaginary Vendor {i:02d} prepares monthly fictional property inspection summaries. Fictional Marketplace Laboratory provides synthetic records only. Both parties designate a review contact. The fee is {1000+i*100}.00 per month, subject to authorized review; this document authorizes no payment.

## Renewal

Renewal is manual and requires a separately reviewed written agreement. There is no automatic renewal.

## Termination

Either fictional party may request termination on 30 days written notice. An authorized legal reviewer must verify the notice period and outstanding obligations.

## Confidentiality

Source documents remain within their authorized department. No party receives access to HR employee files. Generated summaries are drafts for human review.

## Review checklist

Confirm fictional party identities, effective date, service scope, fee calculations, renewal type, termination notice, and department access. This sample is not legal advice or an executable contract.
'''
 path.write_text(text)
 manifest['legal_documents'].append({'path':str(path.relative_to(root)),'title':f'Fictional Service Agreement {i:02d}','expected':{'document_type':'service_agreement','parties':['Fictional Marketplace Laboratory',f'Imaginary Vendor {i:02d}'],'effective_date':'2026-10-01','termination_date':'2027-10-01','renewal_type':'manual','requires_human_review':True}})
properties=[]
for i in range(1,31):
 base={'property_id':f'DEMO-P-{i:04d}','address':f'{100+i} Imaginary Orchard Lane','city':['Fable Springs','Example Harbor','Imaginary Mesa'][i%3],'state':'XX','postal_code':'00000','bedrooms':2+i%4,'bathrooms':1+i%3,'status':'REO','synthetic':True}
 second={'property_id':base['property_id'],'city':base['city'],'bedrooms':base['bedrooms']+(1 if i<=10 else 0),'bathrooms':base['bathrooms']}
 if 11<=i<=20:base.pop('bedrooms');second.pop('bedrooms')
 properties.append({'synthetic':True,'property_id':base['property_id'],'sources':[{'name':'fictional_intake_feed','fields':{k:v for k,v in base.items() if k not in {'synthetic','property_id'}}},{'name':'fictional_review_sheet','fields':{k:v for k,v in second.items() if k != 'property_id'}}],'expected_conflict_fields':['bedrooms'] if i<=10 else [],'expected_missing_fields':['bedrooms'] if 11<=i<=20 else []})
(root/'operations'/'properties.json').write_text(json.dumps(properties,indent=2)+'\n')
(root/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2)+'\n')
(root/'README.md').write_text('''# Synthetic demonstration fixtures

Every person, business, property, invoice and agreement is fictional. The property state `XX` and postal code `00000` are intentionally non-real examples. Historical workflow records created by `app.seed` are explicitly demonstration history, not measured production activity.

`manifest.json` records expected invoice values and document metadata. The reproducible generator is `generate.py`. `make seed` imports these fixtures through the application seeder. The dataset includes 20 PDF invoices, 10 HR policies, 10 legal agreements and 30 properties with multiple source records. Ten properties deliberately conflict on bedroom counts, ten are missing bedrooms, and ten are internally consistent. Invoice amounts use Decimal arithmetic.

All login credentials published in the development realm are public fixture values. Never import these users or files into a real employee-data environment.
''')
